<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TO OFFER 5YR BONDS OF HUF 2BLN ON MARCH 17.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TO OFFER 5YR BONDS OF HUF 2BLN ON MARCH 17.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will offer two</p>
<p>billion forints worth of the five-year government bonds of</p>
<p>2001/C series between March 17 and 21, the Government Debt</p>
<p>Management Agency (AKK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    3 February 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    12 December 2001</p>
<p>    Bills on offer			2,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price		   To be published on March 14</p>
<p>Average price of 2001/C</p>
<p>bonds at last auction (Feb 27) 99.69 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 15.00</p>
<p>percent, payable semi-anually starting from June 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
